# Required Pre-Commit Scripts

Before committing or pushing any change, always run both scripts below and commit any resulting file updates. CI enforces both and will fail (`generate-and-format` / `refresh-and-verify`) if the generated files drift.

## Scripts

- `make dd-refresh-generated` — regenerates `metrics/datadog/*.json` and `metrics/grafana/provisioning/dashboards/*.json` from the live OpenAPI spec.
- `bash scripts/refresh_token_registry.sh` — refreshes `packages/api/src/main/resources/token-registry/main.json` and `test.json` from the upstream registry.

## Workflow

1. Finish the code change.
2. Run `make dd-refresh-generated`.
3. Run `bash scripts/refresh_token_registry.sh`.
4. `git status` — if either step modified tracked files, stage and commit them in the same commit, or in a follow-up `chore:` commit on the same branch, before pushing.

Do not skip these scripts even when the change seems unrelated to API endpoints or tokens — upstream drift can surface on any branch.
